<title>FRANCE: Breakdown of French winter grain sowings estimates.</title>
<headline>Breakdown of French winter grain sowings estimates.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following is a breakdown of winter grain sowing estimates in hectares published by the French farm ministry on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The ministry said the rise in soft wheat sowings was spread across most regions, especially the Champagne-Ardenne region in eastern France, and Pays de Loire and Poitou-Charentes in the west with gains of up to six percent.</p>
<p>Barley sowing increases were strongest in the north, northeast, west and central France with gains of up to 10 percent.</p>
<p>Heavy winter rain in the southeast delayed the completion of durum wheat sowings in traditional areas. At national level the durum wheat area was stabilising.</p>
<p>			    Avg		   Pct  Pct Chg  Pct Chg</p>
<p>			   91-95  1996  1997  sown  97/96  97/91-95</p>
<p> TOTAL WINTER GRAIN   6221  6411  6630   --   3.4	6.6</p>
<p> Soft wheat	     4467  4741  4901  100   3.4	9.7</p>
<p> Durum		     308   263   261   97  -0.9    -15.2</p>
<p> Barley		   1139  1077  1136  100   5.4     -0.2</p>
<p> Oats			 87    77    80  100   5.2     -7.5</p>
<p> Rye			  50    48    48   99  -1.6     -4.9</p>
<p> Triticale		 171   204   204  100  -0.1     19.2</p>
<p>OILSEEDS</p>
<p> Rapeseed		  678   860   931  100   8.3     37.3</p>
<p>NOTES - Figures as of February 1 and in '000 hectares except percentage columns. Source: SCEES, Agriculture Ministry.</p>
